class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> productExceptSelf(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<int> ans(n, 1);

        int prefix = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            ans[i] = prefix;
            prefix *= nums[i];
        }

        int suffix = 1;
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            ans[i] *= suffix;
            suffix *= nums[i];
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
**Intuition:**  
For each element, calculate the product of all elements before and after it.  
Use prefix and suffix products without using division.

**Algorithm:**  
Store prefix products in `ans`, then multiply each position by its suffix product.  
Traverse from both directions to get the final product for every index.

**Complexity:**  
Time: **O(n)**  
Space: **O(1)** extra space (excluding the output array)
